  RELEVANCE: Connects the Anthropology's pragmatic register to the critical framework by locating
  both under the social dimension of the highest good, addressing the domain's key question about
  whether the Anthropology is compatible with transcendental idealism.

  POSITION: Integrative reading that treats the Anthropology as continuous with rather than
  independent of the critical practical philosophy.
  },
  keywords = {kant-philosophy-of-history, highest-good, anthropology, social-character, Medium, INCOMPLETE, no-abstract}
}

@incollection{cohen2009pragmaticAnthropology,
  author = {Cohen, Alix},
  title = {Pragmatic {Anthropology}},
  booktitle = {Kant and the {Human} {Sciences}},
  year = {2009},
  publisher = {Palgrave Macmillan},
  pages = {61--108},
  doi = {10.1057/9780230280779_4},
  note = {
  CORE ARGUMENT: Cohen argues that Kant's pragmatic anthropology occupies a distinctive
  methodological position between empirical psychology (which Kant rejects as a science) and
  transcendental philosophy. The "pragmatic" register --- knowledge of the human being as a free
  agent who can be influenced --- is not a weakened form of empirical knowledge but a legitimate
  domain with its own standards.

  RELEVANCE: Addresses the project's question about the compatibility of the Anthropology's
  pragmatic register with transcendental idealism, providing the clearest account of what
  "pragmatic" means as a methodological category in Kant.

  POSITION: Argues for methodological distinctiveness of pragmatic anthropology, neither fully
  empirical nor transcendental; defends its coherence within the critical system.
  },
  keywords = {kant-philosophy-of-history, anthropology, pragmatic-register, methodology, Medium},
  abstract = {Chapter 3 has shown that Kant's method entails a decisive re-evaluation of traditional enquiries into human nature: it redirects the question, 'what is the human being?' from his passive essence to his active relationship with the world - from what he is to what he does. Accordingly, the remaining task is to redefine our discourse about the human being, thereby inaugurating a new scientific paradigm, that of pragmatic anthropology.},
  abstract_source = {openalex},
}

@article{oh2022pragmaticAnthropologyTeleology,
  author = {Oh, Jaeyoon},
  title = {The {Foundation} of {Kant}'s {Pragmatic} {Anthropology}: {A} {Twofold} {Teleology} of {Nature} and {History}},
  journal = {Korean Journal of Philosophy},
  year = {2022},
